EXT. DRY PLAINS - HIGH NOON - SERIES OF SHOTS

SERIES OF SHOTS:

A) Dust. A long line of people in wide hats and hand-painted signs marching down a dirt road. A banner: THE RIVER IS NOT FOR SALE.

B) Dana, 30s, in a duster coat, leads the march with a megaphone. The sun slams down on her like a hammer.

C) Eli, 20s, thin, carries a drum. Every step, BOOM.

D) Rosa, 50s, wipes her brow with a faded flag. She's done this before.

E) Hank, 60s, in a sheriff's badge, arms crossed beside a rusted oil derrick. His horse noses a tumbleweed.

F) Two teenagers on a fence post film everything on their phones. A coyote watches from the ridge.

G) Tess, 20s, kneels on the road and locks her arm into a barrel of concrete. CLINK.

H) Cole, 40s, in a company suit and cowboy boots, steps out of a black truck. The door SLAMS.

END SERIES OF SHOTS.

EXT. THE OLD PUMP STATION - CONTINUOUS

Cole stops ten feet from Tess. Hank stops beside him. Dana lowers the megaphone. The drum goes quiet.

DANA
You're on public land, Cole.

COLE
Dana. The lease says otherwise.

DANA
Leases can be wrong.

COLE
Not this one.

HANK
(wearily)
Folks. It's a hundred and four degrees.

ROSA
Then you'll want to move that truck.

COLE
I've got a signed order.

ELI
We've got a river.

COLE
You've got a barrel of concrete and a drum.

TESS
And a lot of water bottles.

HANK
Tess, honey, this isn't what I signed up for.

TESS
Sheriff, none of us signed up for the end of the world.

COLE
That's a bit dramatic.

DANA
It's a drought, Cole. Seven years. You want dramatic, go look at Miller's well.

COLE
I've seen Miller's well.

ROSA
Then you know.

COLE
I know there's a hundred jobs on that derrick.

ELI
And a thousand people downriver.

HANK
Cole, they've got a point.

COLE
Hank, whose side are you on?

HANK
I'm on the side with the shade.

A beat. Dana almost laughs.

DANA
Cole. Walk away. Take the order back to the office and tell them the town said no.

COLE
They won't hear it.

DANA
Then make them.

COLE
You don't know what you're asking.

ROSA
We know exactly.

TESS
We're not moving.

ELI
(quietly)
Neither is the river.

A long silence. The wind lifts the banner. The drum, one soft BOOM.

Cole takes off his hat. Looks at the derrick. At the line of faces. At Hank.

COLE
Sheriff. Arrest the barrel.

HANK
Excuse me?

COLE
You heard me. It's a hazard. Roll it off the road.

Dana and Eli lunge in front of Tess. Rosa grabs Hank's sleeve. The two teenagers scream. The coyote bolts. The whole crowd surges forward and then freezes as a siren WAILS in the distance.

Everyone looks at the horizon. A cloud of dust, rolling toward them.
